      "behavior": {
        "inputs": [
          "Command properties, context/flags/hub, target hinted user, parameters and compatibility flag."
        ],
        "preconditions": [],
        "defaults": [
          "UserCommand default ctor sets id/type/context=0; manager accepts exact values without API-level validation except source-side branches described."
        ],
        "effects": [
          "CRUD uses IDs under SharedMutex; find returns -1 when absent; get returns false when absent; move swaps adjacent entries for pos -1/+1 (caller contract asserts those values); update/remove of absent IDs are no-ops. FLAG_NOSAVE commands are not persisted; externally received commands deduplicate and cap at 2000 per hub. userCommand picks a connected command hub or hinted hub, no-ops when user offline, otherwise expands user/hub/my parameters and sends. Listing filters context, protocol and hub/op scope; op output is set true if any selected hub has op status and is otherwise left as passed by caller."
        ],
        "events": [
          "ClientUserCommand obeys HUB_USER_COMMANDS and performs ephemeral add/remove/clear; redirects/disconnects remove external commands. Favorite Load adds built-in NMDC op commands and loads saved XML; Favorite Save serializes saved commands."
        ],
        "errors": [],
        "completion": "Synchronous operations; outbound execution is handed to the selected Client sendUserCmd path.",
        "cancellation": "No cancellation API.",
        "persistence": [
          "FavoriteManager XML stores non-FLAG_NOSAVE command fields; mutations of saved commands mark FavoriteManager dirty."
        ],
        "resources": []
      },
      "ownership_evidence": [],
      "threading_evidence": [],
      "proposed_bridge_requirement": "Use explicit command values and preserve ordering, context, flags and hub association.",
