        "effects": [
          "add creates next ID; externally supplied FLAG_NOSAVE commands are deduplicated by hub/name/context/type/flag/to, replacing command body. More than 2000 external commands per hub causes it to return the current last command rather than append. Saved commands mark FavoriteManager dirty. get searches by ID and copies out. find returns matching name/hub ID or -1. move accepts the intended adjacent positions -1/+1 and swaps on match. update replaces by ID; remove by ID, URL external commands, or context+hub external commands.",
          "userCommand chooses command hub only if a connected client exists, otherwise hinted hub; if target user is not online it does nothing. Otherwise expands user/hub/my parameters and sends via client. Listing filters context and hub schemes; ADC commands match ADC hubs, op-scoped commands require op, chat commands can cross protocol-class filtering. `op` is an output accumulator, not initialized by this method.",
          "Favorite Load inserts built-in NMDC op commands, then loads saved XML. Save serializes only commands without FLAG_NOSAVE. Client hub command input is gated by HUB_USER_COMMANDS and handles remove/clear/add; redirect/disconnect removes ephemeral commands. Manager listens to ClientManager and FavoriteManager for lifetime. SharedMutex guards vector mutations/reads except some edge accesses that remain outside lock."
        ],
